## The packages of nimchoo and what each is for: the first line of the documentation at the top of its
## package.nim (click a name for the rest).  `nch packages` says the same in a terminal, with the dependencies
## (`nch packages --graph` draws them by layer).  The code that every package may use is in `core`.
##
## * `activities <packages/activities/package.html>`_ - The activities: listing them, choosing the selection, and deleting.
## * `args <packages/util/args/package.html>`_ - One command-line parser for all the commands, and the usage text made from the same descriptions.
## * `atomic <packages/util/atomic/package.html>`_ - Writing a file so that nobody ever sees half of it.
## * `bundle <packages/bundle/package.html>`_ - Files built into the program that are also kept in the cache, for the author to edit.
## * `bytes <packages/util/bytes/package.html>`_ - Reading numbers out of bytes, and a whole file as bytes: the one place for it.
## * `cache <packages/cache/package.html>`_ - The cache directory: where files that commands make go, and what they are called.
## * `calendar <packages/calendar/package.html>`_ - A subject on a calendar: by default the days the selected activities started on.
## * `child <packages/util/child/package.html>`_ - Running a child process and collecting what it says.
## * `childasync <packages/util/childasync/package.html>`_ - Running a child process from an event loop, so that other requests are served meanwhile.
## * `climbs <packages/climbs/package.html>`_ - Climbs: found in the rides, named, and ranked.
## * `confirm <packages/confirm/package.html>`_ - Deleting with a pause: the countdown that gives time to press Ctrl-C.
## * `db <packages/db/package.html>`_ - The database: opening it, its schema as fragments, and the statements that touch it.
## * `download <packages/download/package.html>`_ - Fetching what the program needs from the network, the only place it does so.
## * `ff <packages/ff/package.html>`_ - Fitness and fatigue curves from the training impulses.
## * `fit <packages/fit/package.html>`_ - FIT files: the decoder, the profile that says what the fields mean, and `nch fit`.
## * `fold <packages/text/fold/package.html>`_ - Comparing text without regard to case or accents.
## * `geo <packages/geo/package.html>`_ - Flat geometry for rides, in metres.
## * `hashing <packages/util/hashing/package.html>`_ - SHA-256 as the hex text used wherever something is named by its content.
## * `heartrate <packages/heartrate/package.html>`_ - The heart-rate channel of an import.
## * `importer <packages/importer/package.html>`_ - Putting the activities of FIT files into the database, and describing them.
## * `log <packages/log/package.html>`_ - Reading the log: `nch log`.
## * `lookup <packages/util/lookup/package.html>`_ - Table lookups that have to succeed (`must`, `mustMut`).
## * `map <packages/map/package.html>`_ - The map: a view of a subject, drawn from the frames that the packages managing it contribute.
## * `model <packages/model/package.html>`_ - The training impulse: models, and the impulses worked out with them.
## * `names <packages/names/package.html>`_ - Names for places: GeoNames features, and the author's own landmarks.
## * `profiling <packages/util/profiling/package.html>`_ - Timers for finding out where a long job spends its time.
## * `selection <packages/selection/package.html>`_ - The selection: the activities that commands work on unless told otherwise.
## * `subject <packages/subject/package.html>`_ - Subjects: what the views are views of (activities, later climbs and FF statistics).
## * `templating <packages/text/templating/package.html>`_ - Page templates: text with `{{tags}}` filled in from values.
## * `themes <packages/themes/package.html>`_ - The themes in the cache, and which theme is in force.
## * `ui <packages/ui/package.html>`_ - How the program looks: units, intervals, styles and themes, tables and the live display.
## * `user <packages/user/package.html>`_ - The users, and which one a command works for.
## * `version <packages/util/version/package.html>`_ - What `nch --version` says: the version in nimchoo.nimble and the git commit it was built from.
## * `warnings <packages/util/warnings/package.html>`_ - Warnings: oddities in a file that do not stop us reading it.
## * `web <packages/web/package.html>`_ - The local web server: runs `nch` commands named in addresses and shows their pages.
## * `xlsx <packages/util/xlsx/package.html>`_ - A minimal xlsx reader: the cell values of worksheets, as strings.
## * `zip <packages/util/zip/package.html>`_ - Reading zip files: the entries of a zip in memory, and inflating one in a child process.

